   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th testicular tumours & AJCC 8th pT1a/pT1b staging",
    "intro": "WHO 5th separates germ cell tumours into GCNIS-derived vs non-GCNIS-derived, replaces PNET with embryonic-type neuroectodermal tumour (ENET), defines somatic-type malignancy using a >= 5 mm pure nodule threshold, and replaces 'carcinoid' with prepubertal-type testicular NET.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Key staging & immunohistochemistry landmarks",
      "points": [
       "Pure seminoma confined to testis without LVI: < 30 mm = pT1a; >= 30 mm = pT1b (note: non-seminomas do not split pT1a/b).",
       "Hilar soft tissue invasion, epididymal invasion, visceral tunica vaginalis perforation, or LVI = pT2; direct spermatic cord soft tissue invasion = pT3 (LVI alone in cord is pT2, not pT3); scrotum = pT4.",
       "IHC panel: Seminoma (OCT3/4+, SALL4+, CD117+, D2-40+, CD30-); Embryonal (OCT3/4+, SALL4+, CD30+, AE1/AE3+); Yolk sac (SALL4+, glypican-3+, AFP+, OCT3/4-); Choriocarcinoma (beta-hCG+, GATA3+, SALL4 variable)."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Testicular Germ Cell Tumors",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
